  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return []\n    H = len(grid)\n    W = len(grid[0])\n\n    # Determine separator color from first row\n    bg = grid[0][0]\n    sep_color = None\n    for c in range(1, W):\n        if grid[0][c] != bg:\n            sep_color = grid[0][c]\n            break\n    if sep_color is None:\n        # Fallback: check first column\n        for r in range(1, H):\n            if grid[r][0] != bg:\n                sep_color = grid[r][0]\n                break\n    if sep_color is None:\n        return grid\n\n    # Find regularly spaced separator lines\n    v_seps = [c for c in range(W) if grid[0][c] == sep_color]\n    h_seps = [r for r in range(H) if grid[r][0] == sep_color]\n\n    # Locate bounding box of non-separator values at grid intersections\n    active_is = []\n    active_js = []\n    for i, r in enumerate(h_seps):\n        for j, c in enumerate(v_seps):\n            if grid[r][c] != sep_color:\n                active_is.append(i)\n                active_js.append(j)\n\n    if not active_is:\n        return grid\n\n    min_i = min(active_is)\n    max_i = max(active_is)\n    min_j = min(active_js)\n    max_j = max(active_js)\n\n    # Extract the intersection subgrid\n    inter = []\n    for i in range(min_i, max_i + 1):\n        row = []\n        for j in range(min_j, max_j + 1):\n            row.append(grid[h_seps[i]][v_seps[j]])\n        inter.append(row)\n\n    # Each output cell corresponds to a 2x2 block of intersections\n    out_h = max_i - min_i\n    out_w = max_j - min_j\n    out = [[0] * out_w for _ in range(out_h)]\n\n    for i in range(out_h):\n        for j in range(out_w):\n            a = inter[i][j]\n            b = inter[i][j + 1]\n            c = inter[i + 1][j]\n            d = inter[i + 1][j + 1]\n            if a == b == c == d and a != sep_color:\n                out[i][j] = a\n            else:\n                out[i][j] = 0\n\n    return out\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return []\n    H = len(grid)\n    W = len(grid[0])\n\n    # Determine separator color from first row\n    bg = grid[0][0]\n    sep_color = None\n    for c in range(1, W):\n        if grid[0][c] != bg:\n            sep_color = grid[0][c]\n            break\n    if sep_color is None:\n        # Fallback: check first column\n        for r in range(1, H):\n            if grid[r][0] != bg:\n                sep_color = grid[r][0]\n                break\n    if sep_color is None:\n        return grid\n\n    # Find regularly spaced separator lines\n    v_seps = [c for c in range(W) if grid[0][c] == sep_color]\n    h_seps = [r for r in range(H) if grid[r][0] == sep_color]\n\n    # Locate bounding box of non-separator values at grid intersections\n    active_is = []\n    active_js = []\n    for i, r in enumerate(h_seps):\n        for j, c in enumerate(v_seps):\n            if grid[r][c] != sep_color:\n                active_is.append(i)\n                active_js.append(j)\n\n    if not active_is:\n        return grid\n\n    min_i = min(active_is)\n    max_i = max(active_is)\n    min_j = min(active_js)\n    max_j = max(active_js)\n\n    # Extract the intersection subgrid\n    inter = []\n    for i in range(min_i, max_i + 1):\n        row = []\n        for j in range(min_j, max_j + 1):\n            row.append(grid[h_seps[i]][v_seps[j]])\n        inter.append(row)\n\n    # Each output cell corresponds to a 2x2 block of intersections\n    out_h = max_i - min_i\n    out_w = max_j - min_j\n    out = [[0] * out_w for _ in range(out_h)]\n\n    for i in range(out_h):\n        for j in range(out_w):\n            a = inter[i][j]\n            b = inter[i][j + 1]\n            c = inter[i + 1][j]\n            d = inter[i + 1][j + 1]\n            if a == b == c == d and a != sep_color:\n                out[i][j] = a\n            else:\n                out[i][j] = 0\n\n    return out",
